<task id="020" project="ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Session↔Analysis binding FK + standardize on ChatEndpoints</title>
    <phase>2 Session</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies BFF session persistence (`Sprk.Bff.Api`) + Dataverse write path; tags bff/dataverse/session; core data-spine seam every Phase 2/3 task depends on.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Bounded modification of a known repository/manager path against a verified schema contract; no architectural authoring — Sonnet @ high suffices.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Serial within Phase 2 — shares session code (`ChatSessionManager`/`ChatDataverseRepository`) with 021/022/023/025 and collides with `Services/Ai/` (redesign-r2 sole owner); `/conflict-check` before the BFF PR.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>010,011</deps>
    <tags>bff, dataverse, session</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Bind chat sessions to the owner-created `sprk_aichatsummary → sprk_analysis` lookup FK: write the analysis FK
    inside `ChatDataverseRepository.CreateSessionAsync` alongside the existing `sprk_sessionid` grouping key, so an
    Analysis-owned session carries its Analysis reference and "one Analysis → many sessions" is queryable by
    `sprk_sessionid` + the analysis FK. Standardize on the `ChatEndpoints` (Redis→Cosmos→Dataverse-anchor) path.
    MUST NOT write the dead `sprk_analysischatmessage` entity.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the BFF chat/session persistence tiers (Redis→Cosmos→Dataverse anchor),
    `ChatDataverseRepository` sessionId grouping, and the ADR-013 `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` facade. Follow ADRs strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `ChatDataverseRepository.CreateSessionAsync` writes the `sprk_analysis` FK on the `sprk_aichatsummary` record
    for Analysis-owned sessions; sessions for a given Analysis are retrievable by the analysis FK (grouped by
    `sprk_sessionid`); the dead `sprk_analysischatmessage` entity is never written; build + tests green; publish-size
    reported ≤60 MB with no new HIGH CVE.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Verified session facts: GUIDs are minted 100% server-side at `ChatSessionManager.cs:108` (`Guid.NewGuid`);
      the create endpoint is `ChatEndpoints.cs:345`; per-turn history writes to `sprk_chathistory` at
      `ChatEndpoints.cs:956` keyed on `session.HostContext.EntityType="sprk_analysisoutput"`+`EntityId`;
      `sprk_sessionid` is the grouping key (`ChatDataverseRepository.cs:37-45,128-137`). The owner has pre-created the
      `sprk_aichatsummary → sprk_analysis` lookup (verified present by task 010). Storage model is ADR-040 Path A:
      Cosmos = durable transcript store-of-record, Dataverse `sprk_analysis`/`sprk_aichatsummary` = business anchor.
      This task adds the last-mile FK write; it does NOT introduce a new entity or a second session store.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/ChatDataverseRepository.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/ChatDataverseRepository.cs (lines 37-45, 128-137 — sessionId grouping)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/ChatSessionManager.cs (line 108 — server-minted GUID)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Endpoints/ChatEndpoints.cs (lines 345 create, 956 per-turn history)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (session repository tests)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">Owner schema preflight — `sprk_aichatsummary.sprk_analysis` FK confirmed present.</dependency>
      <dependency task="011" status="pending">Client `sprk_analysis` TypeScript type (analysisId shape consumed downstream).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">SCOPE: session persistence writes. Cosmos remains the transcript store-of-record; the Dataverse `sprk_aichatsummary`/`sprk_analysis` write is the business anchor only — do NOT create a second transcript store or move per-message durability into Dataverse (Path A project exception).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">SCOPE: this BFF write path. Reach any AI capability through `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`; MUST NOT inject AI-internal types into the session repository or fork `Services/Ai/` (sole-owned by redesign-r2).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: the Dataverse write in `CreateSessionAsync`. MUST NOT revive or write the dead `sprk_analysischatmessage` entity (empty shell — §11 reuse violation); bind ONLY to `sprk_aichatsummary` + the new `sprk_analysis` FK.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: session path selection. Standardize on `ChatEndpoints` (Redis→Cosmos); MUST NOT extend the deprecated `AnalysisEndpoints` in-memory session model.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">SCOPE: this BFF-touching task. State the Placement Justification (modification of existing repository path), run `dotnet publish -c Release`, report compressed size + diff vs ~49.63 MB baseline (≤60 MB), and confirm no new HIGH CVE from `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">SCOPE: any endpoint touched. Session create/read stays behind Spaarke Auth v2; an unauthenticated caller MUST get 401, not an anonymous session.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>BFF chat/session persistence + Dataverse write path</topic>
