  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor + reason; load knowledge files; confirm task 010 verified the `sprk_aichatsummary.sprk_analysis` FK present.</step>
    <step order="1">Read `ChatDataverseRepository.cs` (37-45, 128-137) + `ChatSessionManager.cs:108` + `ChatEndpoints.cs:345,956` to map the current create + sessionId-grouped write.</step>
    <step order="2">Extend `CreateSessionAsync` to set the `sprk_analysis` lookup on the `sprk_aichatsummary` record when the session is Analysis-owned (analysisId supplied via HostContext), alongside the existing `sprk_sessionid`.</step>
    <step order="3">Add/confirm a read path that returns sessions for a given Analysis (filter by the analysis FK, grouped by `sprk_sessionid`) — "one Analysis → many sessions".</step>
    <step order="4">Verify no code path writes `sprk_analysischatmessage`; confirm the write stays on the `ChatEndpoints` (Redis→Cosmos→anchor) path and does not touch `AnalysisEndpoints`.</step>
    <step order="5">Add/update unit tests: FK is written for an Analysis-owned session; query-by-analysis-FK returns the grouped sessions; loose (no analysisId) session writes no FK; dead entity never written.</step>
    <step order="6">`/conflict-check` vs `spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2`; then `dotnet build` + `dotnet test`; run `dotnet publish -c Release` and record compressed size + diff + CVE scan in task notes.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set 020 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If binding the FK appears to require modifying `Services/Ai/` internals (not just composing `PublicContracts/` seams + the Dataverse write), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6.5 — `Services/Ai/` is sole-owned by redesign-r2 (no fork).</trigger>
    <trigger>If task 010 finds the `sprk_aichatsummary.sprk_analysis` FK NOT present, STOP — this task is gated on the owner schema and cannot proceed.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
