  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an Analysis-owned session (analysisId in HostContext), when `CreateSessionAsync` runs, then the `sprk_aichatsummary` record carries the `sprk_analysis` FK plus its `sprk_sessionid`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an Analysis with multiple sessions, when queried by the analysis FK, then all its sessions are returned grouped by `sprk_sessionid` ("one Analysis → many sessions").</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no code path writes the dead `sprk_analysischatmessage` entity (grep-clean + test asserts it is never written).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a loose session (no analysisId) writes NO analysis FK; the record persists with only `sprk_sessionid`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an unauthenticated call to the session create/read endpoint returns 401, not an anonymous session.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Session writes stay on the `ChatEndpoints` path; `AnalysisEndpoints` in-memory session model is not extended.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish-size ≤60 MB compressed (diff vs ~49.63 MB reported); no new HIGH CVE; all unit tests pass; build green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec.md FR-05. This is the data-spine seam; keep the FK write minimal and on the live `sprk_aichatsummary` path.
    Tasks 021 (fork) and 031 (reopen) consume "query sessions by analysis FK". `/conflict-check` before the BFF PR.

    ## Completion note (2026-07-28)

    STATUS: completed. Ground truth re-verified live via Dataverse MCP `describe('tables/sprk_aichatsummary')`
    immediately before implementation: `sprk_analysis LOOKUP (GUID) (Related table: sprk_analysis)` — confirms
    task 010's finding and the exact attribute/target-entity names used below.

    ### Implementation
    - `ChatDataverseRepository.CreateSessionAsync` (Services/Ai/Chat/): when
      `session.HostContext?.EntityType == "sprk_analysisoutput"` and `HostContext.EntityId` parses as a GUID
      (the existing convention `ChatEndpoints.cs` SendMessageAsync already uses for the `sprk_chathistory` write),
      sets `entity["sprk_analysis"] = new EntityReference("sprk_analysis", analysisId)` alongside the existing
      `sprk_sessionid` write. Loose (non-Analysis) sessions write no FK — unchanged behavior otherwise.
    - New read method `IChatDataverseRepository.GetSessionsByAnalysisAsync(string tenantId, Guid analysisId, ct)`
      — `QueryExpression` on `sprk_aichatsummary` filtered by `sprk_analysis` AND `sprk_tenantid` (tenant-scoped
      per ADR-014/ADR-028, added during code-review — every sibling read method on the interface takes tenantId;
      the first draft omitted it), projecting into a new `AnalysisSessionSummary` record
      (`SessionId, MessageCount, IsArchived, CreatedOn`). Each returned row already represents exactly one
      session (`CreateSessionAsync` writes one row per session) — "one Analysis → many sessions" is satisfied
      by the query returning N rows, no further server-side grouping needed.
    - New file: `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Models/Ai/Chat/AnalysisSessionSummary.cs` (24-line DTO).
    - `sprk_analysischatmessage` — confirmed grep-clean across `src/` (only appears in docs/notes/other-project
      POMLs referencing its retirement); never written by this or any other code path; test asserts it too.
    - `AnalysisEndpoints` (legacy in-memory path) — not touched.

    ### Placement Justification (root CLAUDE.md §10 / `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`)
    Modification of an EXISTING repository (`ChatDataverseRepository`) and its EXISTING interface
    (`IChatDataverseRepository`) — not a new service, endpoint, DI registration, or package. Belongs in BFF
    per ADR-013 (session persistence is already BFF-hosted; this is the last-mile FK write on that existing
    write path). No new CRUD→AI dependency introduced (this repository does not call any AI service — ADR-002,
    unchanged). `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §11 Component Justification for the ONE new file
    (`AnalysisSessionSummary.cs`): existing = grep-verified no equivalent DTO exists; extension = the read path
    requires a typed projection, none of the existing `ChatSession`/`ChatMessage` shapes fit a lightweight
    multi-row summary; cost-of-doing-nothing = without a read method, acceptance criterion #2 ("one Analysis →
    many sessions" queryable) is unmet and tasks 021/031 have no query surface to consume.

    ### Quality gates (Step 9.5)
    - `code-review`: reviewed diff directly (metrics, AI-smell checklist, ADR/§11 justification, 17-ban test
      check). Found and FIXED one Warning during review: `GetSessionsByAnalysisAsync` initially omitted
      `tenantId` — inconsistent with every sibling method on `IChatDataverseRepository` and a tenant-isolation
      gap (ADR-014/ADR-028). Fixed by adding the parameter + `sprk_tenantid` filter condition before finalizing;
      tests updated to assert both conditions. No other Critical/Warning findings. Test-shape check against the
      17-ban list (tests/CLAUDE.md): the new `ChatDataverseRepositoryTests.cs` mocks `IGenericEntityService` only
      (the Dataverse SDK boundary — matches `NotificationServiceTests.cs`/`DataverseObservationMirrorTests.cs`
      precedent and the allowed-seam guidance in `src/server/shared/CLAUDE.md`), asserts real field/shape values
      (not interaction-only `Verify(Times.Once)`), and is not a mirror/pass-through/coverage-filler test — no
      ban triggered. Location note (non-blocking): the file sits at
      `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/Chat/` rather than one of the 7 canonical KEEP paths in
      tests/CLAUDE.md; this matches the ~67 existing sibling files at the same location using the identical
      Mock-boundary pattern (the KEEP-path migration sweep is explicitly acknowledged as incomplete/phased in
      tests/CLAUDE.md) — flagged for the eventual sweep, not new debt introduced by this task.
    - `adr-check`: 0 Violations, 0 Warnings after the tenantId fix. Compliant: ADR-002 (no AI processing —
      unchanged), ADR-010 (no new DI registrations), ADR-013 (Dataverse-persistence-only change, no orchestration
      fork, no new CRUD→AI dependency), ADR-040 (Cosmos remains transcript store-of-record; this write is the
      business anchor only — Path A per project CLAUDE.md), ADR-014/ADR-028 (tenant-scoped read, fixed above).
    - `/conflict-check`: ran `git diff --name-only origin/master...HEAD` + `gh pr list --state open --json
      number,title,headRefName,files` (23 open PRs). Zero overlap on `ChatDataverseRepository.cs`,
      `IChatDataverseRepository.cs`, `AnalysisSessionSummary.cs`, or any `Services/Ai/Chat/**` file. Confirmed
      `spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2` (sole owner of `Services/Ai/` internals per `projects/INDEX.md`) has
      no open PR touching these files; this project's own `projects/INDEX.md` row already documents this exact
      FK-binding scope as pre-cleared (BFF=Y note). Safe to proceed — no coordination action needed.

